! IslandAdaptor — Invariant

!! Identity

`IslandAdaptor` provides the narrow TS shore between `CompositeStore` and the wiki.
It implements `MemeProjection` (inbound) and exposes `saveTiddler` / `deleteTiddler` (outbound).
It does NOT implement the TW5 `syncadaptor` module contract — `$tw.syncer` does not run. The outbound bridge (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/outbound-bridge.ts`, stood per island in `sovereign-kernel.ts`) reads every live `$tw.wiki` `change` dispatch for it ([[outbound-bridge|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/outbound-bridge]]).

Under the yin-collapse law (lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/nalu), the wiki IS the
reactive engine. The adaptor holds the shore work that TW5 cannot do from inside itself:
subscribing to the CompositeStore projection bus, queueing each inbound change and landing it as
the composition resolves it, keeping the account of what each wave left, and carrying a hand's
edit to the store with its base. The law it enacts stands at
`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/outbound-bridge#/the-shore-law`; this carrier names the adaptor's
own invariants and no more.

!! Responsibility Split

| Concern | Owner |
|---|---|
| Subscribe to CompositeStore projection bus | IslandAdaptor (`start`) |
| The ordered landing queue, its 200-change slices, the host-task yield between them, the seed checkpoint | IslandAdaptor through `WaveLanding` (`wave-landing.ts`) |
| The queue's door at `$tw.lares.enqueueNalu` | IslandAdaptor (`installLandingQueue`; removed at `stop`) |
| Resolve a bagged change through the composition (`store.resolveLayered`) | IslandAdaptor (`_landOne`) |
| Apply ONE change to the wiki | nalu-engine (`$tw.lares.applyNalu`, in-wiki) |
| The landed ledger: per title the value, bag and heads the last wave left | IslandAdaptor (`LandedLedger`, `landed-ledger.ts`) |
| Read a live wiki `change` dispatch: discrete acts first, then foam or a hand per title | the outbound bridge (`outbound-bridge.ts`) |
| Pace a hand per title (trailing window + non-resetting cap), flush at teardown | IslandAdaptor through `HandGate` (`hand-gate.ts`) |
| Outbound save → the meme family through `store.writeFamily` in the layer the cascade names at or above the working layer, or the higher layer where the title already lives | IslandAdaptor (`_saveBag`, `_writeMeme`) |
| Outbound delete → `tombstoneInBag` in the bag the composition's layer order picks | IslandAdaptor (`_tombstoneBag`) |
| A draft's target, wanted title and draft-open base | IslandAdaptor (the draft book, `draft-book.ts`) |
| Echo guard for a synchronous caller during an apply | `$tw.lares.isApplyingNalu()` |

!! Wiring — One Projection, One Door

```typescript
const adaptor = new IslandAdaptor(tw5, composite, wikiSlug);
adaptor.installLandingQueue();
adaptor.start();
```

No accumulator. No `flushAll`. The adaptor owns the queue and the door; the wiki's nalu engine owns the apply.

!! Invariants

''I-1 Every envelope reads as a wave.''
`onUriChanged` queues every change, this shore's own writes included. An own-origin envelope
(`origin.kind === "tw-local"` with this `instanceId`) counts as the store's acknowledgment of the
write, and its `writtenAt` heads become the base the hand's next write builds on. No origin filter
decides what lands; the landed ledger does.

''I-2 The wiki shows what the composition resolves.''
A bagged change lands the record `store.resolveLayered(title)` answers: the topmost layer holding any
record for the title, a tombstone included (the ''kāpae'' semantics), with that layer's bag and
heads. A tombstone in a higher-priority bag SHADOWS the bags beneath it and the wiki title reads
gone; a lower layer's record never lands over a higher layer's; where no layer holds a record the
title lands absent. Only an unbagged change lands its own record. (the shadow-vs-fall-through cut: [[kapae|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae]])

''I-3 Single forwarding path for all origins.''
Every inbound change — `crdt-remote`, `canon-hydrate`, `lares-verb`, `tw-local` — flows through
the one landing queue. No origin gets special-cased to bypass it. Seed replay and live changes share
the queue and its slices.

''I-4 Outbound save.''
`saveTiddler` refuses a title that never persists (`neverPersists`: the volatile VM plane and the
alert rail, ahead of any cascade edit), teaches the draft book when the tiddler carries `draft.of`,
and marks the title in the hand gate. The flush reads the title's state in the wiki (a direct caller that hands in a tiddler the wiki does not hold rides pinned, its value standing in), routes BY KIND
through the cascade (`lar-bag-paths.tid`): a `draft.of` tiddler to the draft slot, `$:/temp/*` and
most `$:/state/*` to the temp store, the personal kind to the personal slot, the catch-all to
`current-wiki-bag`. `_settle` accepts only a layer the composition mounts at or above the working
layer and refuses every other answer by name (`UnroutedSaveRefusal`, raised on the alert rail). The
write reaches `store.writeFamily()` via the Path-H auto-split (`splitBodyTiddler`), carrying its base.

''I-5 Outbound delete.''
`deleteTiddler` refuses a title that never persists and marks the title like a save. A delete
routes LIKE A SAVE, and the tiddler has left the wiki by then, so no field answers: the bag of this shore's own last acknowledged write of the title answers first, then the landed ledger's bag,
a title never seen this session falls to the cascade's title read, and `_tombstoneBag` picks the bag by the composition's layer order (the landed layer at or
above the working layer; else where a save of the title would land; else the working layer). The
tombstone lands through `tombstoneInBag` with its base, then ahu fragment-parent children
get removed from the wiki directly (outbound housekeeping). A composition with no working layer
refuses the delete by name.

''I-6 onSyncComplete is observability-only.''
The shore keeps no per-island pre-sync buffer. The method exists for
projection-protocol compatibility and may carry future telemetry; it does not
mutate adaptor or wiki state.

''I-7 onChangeset enters the queue as one grain.''
A changeset carries the complete envelopes of whole store changes: a local family write, or the union of
the change events the provider gathered for a bag, whatever its size. The adaptor hands it to the landing
queue as ONE family (`enqueueFamily`), and the queue lands it inside one slice.

''I-8 A stopped shore holds no account of the wiki.''
`stop()` awaits acts in flight, stops the queue, flushes every marked hand, removes the door it
installed, and clears the ledger, the sent values, the hand bases, the last-write bags and the
unlanded marks. A restart seeds afresh and turns resident at its own seed checkpoint.

!! The seed

The recipe (`buildIslandRecipe`) installs the landing queue and starts the adaptor, then drives
`AutomergeDocStore.emitInitialReplay()` per bag. Each existing record flows through
the provider → `adaptor.onUriChanged` → the landing queue.
The recipe then arms the seed checkpoint (`armSeedCheckpoint`), which resolves once the queue and
its tracked work settle and turns the shore resident (a seed landing that fails twice rejects it); the kernel awaits it before `behavior.onEa` runs.

